<div class="prose"><p>A recorded transition lets a later session recover what changed and which conditions were met. A software revision may be accepted before anyone deploys it. Each state belongs to its declared subject.</p>
<p>A machine-agent instance belongs to one session and ends with it. Its working memory is temporary. Durable continuity comes from saved Project State, through a <strong>Context View</strong> prepared for the task and an <strong>Ontology View</strong> of relevant concepts and connections.</p>
<p>Task view {{CASE_VIEW_VERSION}} was usable when this investigation began. At a later checkpoint its period of use has ended, so the agent pauses until a newly checked view and current permission are available. A new session starts with empty working memory and recovers the saved assessment, candidate proposal and owner decisions through current views.</p>
<p>The incident record’s lifecycle is active, while its response closure field remains open. A closure decision follows the incident’s governing Policy and preserves uncertainty and follow-up obligations. Recovery may be evidenced while the cause remains unresolved.</p></div>
